WEBVTT

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:05.480
I suppose I really am cursed.

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:10.240
My memories with you exist only within myself.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.990
If I let them go, then all of it
will be just an illusion...

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:17.280
But that's fine.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:33.590
After-School Pleiades

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:39.760
Sobbingly, I went on my journey

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:44.230
Wishing I could at least fly through the sky

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:50.610
And yet the stars gently shone on me in the nights after our quarrels

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:56.160
I wonder if you were also watching them

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:01.410
I don't know... I want to know... I want to feel it...

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:08.460
Nothingness simply means there are infinite possibilities

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:12.260
The excitement I got after realizing that

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:15.340
was like surfing the waves of space and time

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:20.430
How strange that I'm not afraid anymore

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:23.140
Let's embrace our imperfections and go on

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.020
We'll open the promised door

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:31.190
and gain dazzling smiles!

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:53.760
If I wait for Minato, will he come?

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:58.340
I need to tell him about me...

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:04.180
H-Huh?

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:06.770
I transformed by myself again!

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:08.690
Are the fragments—

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:16.690
Shining Night

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:25.120
I'm taking back what belongs to me.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:29.460
Magic user, are you alone today?

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:30.170
Huh?

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:32.090
Um, Mina—

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.300
It can't be...

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:43.430
Subaru?

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:44.850
What was that alarm just now?

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.100
Everyone...

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:47.980
Y-You!

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:49.350
Why do you have the fragments?

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:00.150
Stop! Give back our fragments!

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:02.370
A fragment!

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:03.410
I know!

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.280
No, there's another fragment!

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.290
This makes eleven.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:15.290
The other ten fragments are ours.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.340
What?

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.300
The twelfth one?

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:20.800
He's drawing it toward him.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:22.890
Bad, bad, very bad!

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:24.180
We need to hurry!

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:25.600
Subaru!

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:28.850
What do I do? This is my fault.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:31.770
No one could have predicted this.

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:32.520
That's right.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:33.690
You can be upset later.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:35.730
Recovering the fragments comes first!

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:37.570
Yeah.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.320
Just wait, you thieving horned man!

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:47.910
H-Huh?

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.290
Why is this...

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:59.800
Your power was being amplified
by the fragments you'd collected.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:03.550
With the fragments stolen from you,
that effect has been nullified.

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:06.890
In other words, we're back where we started?

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:08.430
That's disheartening.

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:10.600
It was all just the fragments' blessing?

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:11.600
What do we do?

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:13.810
If we don't hurry, we'll be too late!

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:18.400
The reappearance of the combined drive shaft?

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.440
This should allow us to pursue him!

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:22.740
But that only seats one, right?

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.200
Then I'll—

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:25.950
I want to go.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:30.580
I have to talk to him, or else I...

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:32.710
Subaru, why?

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:34.830
That boy

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:36.830
was Minato.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:41.260
Minato? Your flowerbed sweetheart?

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:42.220
What do you mean?

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:43.340
What are you saying?

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:45.840
You mean he took advantage of your pure heart?

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:47.600
Aoi...

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.310
All the more reason you can't, then.

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:51.180
Sending you alone would be too dangerous.

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:52.520
Please.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:56.480
I'll get our fragments back,
no matter what happens!

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:00.270
Okay,

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:02.320
if you insist, Subarun.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:04.360
But be very careful, okay?

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:05.740
Bon voyage.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:06.990
Everyone...

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:08.280
Thank you!

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:11.950
Make sure you come back safely.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.080
Okay.

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:30.220
A Tale of Space and Constellations

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:32.970
Hey!

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:35.350
Time for lights out.

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:37.600
What if your fever comes back?

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:39.150
I'll be fine.

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:43.360
Mom and Dad worry so much because
you make a big fuss out of it like that.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:48.320
A Tale of Space and Constellations

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:47.740
You'll be discharged next week,
so bear with it a little longer.

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:50.660
Goodnight, Minato.

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:52.370
Goodnight.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:57.420
Discharge
Day\h\h!

00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:59.880
I want to go home soon.

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.520
There it is.

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:19.270
I'm on a roll today.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:21.020
What's that?

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:25.530
What's that?

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:28.320
You can see me?

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:33.530
That's uncommon for humans who
have matured as much as you.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:37.290
It means you still have a star in your heart.

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:42.250
Well?

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:45.630
How do I appear to you?

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:48.010
How?

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:51.470
Like a boy around my age?

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:52.850
I see.

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:55.680
Hey, have you seen a star?

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:57.680
A star?

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:00.940
Oh, yeah... A few days ago...

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:04.190
Yes. That was our spaceship.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:06.440
Spaceship? That meteor shower?

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:12.990
Right now, our engine's broken and
we're leaking energy, so we're in a bind.

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:17.620
<i>He told me he was an alien who had</i>

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:20.710
<i>come to Earth alone to repair his broken spaceship.</i>

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:25.960
Well, currently, this is the most we can retrieve.

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:26.920
What's that?

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:30.010
This shiny object is what we
call "crystallized potential."

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:32.720
It's the energy source for our spaceship.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:36.560
They turned into that meteor shower
and rained down on Earth,

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:38.470
coming to reside in people's hearts.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:40.980
"Crystallized potential"?

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:43.850
Well, I need to get going.

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:46.230
I can't keep wasting time.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.150
Let me help, too!

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:50.650
I'd appreciate that, but...

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:52.740
Don't you need to sleep?

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:53.990
I'm fine!

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:55.200
Hmm...

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:57.740
All right, then.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:11.170
Hey, could you give me a name?

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:11.920
A name?

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:14.640
Not having one is inconvenient, right?

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:17.390
Oh. Um...

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:17.430
A Tale of Space and Constellations

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:22.560
Then how about Elnath?

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:24.270
It's the second star of Taurus.

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:28.150
Does that make you the first star, Aldebaran?

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:33.110
I didn't mean it that way... But you're
not really an "Aldebaran" type, right?

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:38.080
I guess so. So what is your real name?

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:40.580
It's Minato!

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:42.250
I see. Minato.

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:43.620
Then come with me.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:46.460
But that's a window.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:49.500
That doesn't matter to us.

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:56.390
<i>He led me</i>

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:00.310
<i>out of that dark hospital room.</i>

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:06.310
<i>To me, he was my first friend.</i>

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:12.030
<i>Every night afterward, we went around
gathering the shiny lights.</i>

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:17.280
<i>Strangely enough, no one could ever see us.</i>

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:24.290
Our spaceship is both matter and
energy, yet also neither.

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:27.460
It's what we call a superposition.

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:29.130
A superposition?

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:33.260
Yes. It exists as countless overlapping potentials.

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:37.130
In that sense, humans are also
much like our spaceship.

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:40.510
The young ones in particular,
the younger they are,

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:45.390
are as yet nothing, wavering
between many potentials.

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:47.940
Those potentials are nurtured in their hearts,

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:51.020
and once their host finally becomes something,

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:55.400
the object expelled along with all their lost potentials

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:57.320
is this shiny thing.

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:59.410
What happens once it's expelled?

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:03.660
They disappear, never amounting to anything.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:07.710
<i>"Crystallized potential,"</i>

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:12.000
<i>those fated to disappear,
without ever being chosen.</i>

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:15.800
<i>They seemed dear to me, somehow.</i>

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:19.550
All right, let's call it a night.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:20.390
Okay.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:27.310
What's wrong?

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:29.020
Someone's watching us.

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:33.480
That can't be. No one can see us.

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:39.150
<i>On that day...</i>

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:44.240
<i>You appeared</i>

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:48.870
<i>in my little universe.</i>

00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:58.300
Why did you come here, nobody?

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:02.180
<i>I knew it.</i>

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:05.060
<i>He doesn't recognize me in this form.</i>

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:09.100
Give those back!

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:12.610
We're the ones who gathered
those engine fragments.

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:14.520
So please give them back, Mina—

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.490
You mean to steal the fragments from me?

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:21.990
Each of those fragments is precious to us!

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:25.410
Let go!

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:28.540
They're filled with everyone's...
With our memories!

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:34.960
Gathering the fragments for that alien is ridiculous.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:41.300
I wonder if Subaru's all right.

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:42.510
Yeah.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.300
Aoi, what are you doing?

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:48.270
Well, I can't just sit still!

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:52.190
Subaru's out there, trying hard
by herself, and I'm here...

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:57.020
That doesn't mean you should make one so long...

00:11:57.020 --> 00:11:59.530
It is a bit nerve-wracking.

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:01.780
Hey, Itsuki, you'll stretch out the president!

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:03.570
Ah! I'm sorry!

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:08.200
Subaru will be fine.

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:11.540
I'm sure she'll bring the fragments back to us.

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:13.500
Yeah, you're right.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:16.670
That's right! We have to
have faith and wait for her!

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:17.630
Yeah.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:22.680
That alien is just a coward.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:26.680
Once he knew there was no choice
left that would save them,

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:29.470
he abandoned the act of choosing itself.

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:32.810
He's putting the problem off, unable to act.

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:34.810
Why do you say that?

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:38.570
Well, I'm in no place to talk about them...

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:39.820
Huh?

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:43.950
I'm going to use these to search
for a different world.

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:45.950
A different world?

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:51.160
If this world won't accept me,
then I'll abandon it myself.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:53.910
I'll take along all those who,

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:59.500
just like me, were never given
any kind of potential here...

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:02.460
The world will be glad to have us gone.

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:04.300
What do you mean?

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:07.180
Where are you going?

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.850
I'm going to disappear.

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:26.950
It's pretty!

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:34.410
What's that?

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:40.670
<i>That girl was at the hospital, visiting her
mother, when she apparently got lost.</i>

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:47.430
Last night, I wished on a shooting star
that Mom would get better soon.

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:50.680
It was a pretty shooting star...

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:54.100
But my dad told me there
wasn't any shooting star.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:57.520
That was you?

00:13:57.520 --> 00:13:58.310
Huh?

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:02.230
That shooting star was me. Watch.

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:19.250
It's all right. I can use magic.

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:21.340
Magic?

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:24.840
<i>My encounter with that girl gave me hope.</i>

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:28.050
<i>The shiny objects spilling
from the hearts of others...</i>

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:30.800
<i>She thought I was a shooting
star as I flew around,</i>

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:34.680
<i>gathering them every night,
and she made a wish upon me.</i>

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:38.850
<i>For the first time, I thought I might
be able to grant someone's wish,</i>

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:46.440
<i>that I might be useful to someone,
that I might be able to protect someone.</i>

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:51.870
Wow, what's that?

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:54.030
That's a fragment of our engine.

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:54.870
It is?

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:59.750
That holds enough power to change our destinies.

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:03.040
Right now, it's far beyond our reach, though.

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:08.050
If I had that, I could grant that girl's wish, as well.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:09.470
That girl?

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:11.430
What? What are you planning to do?

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:14.390
I'm going to capture it! I can do it now!

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:18.350
Stop! You're planning to use that
power on one individual's wish?

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:21.600
The truth is that you also need it, don't you?

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:25.980
We've already gathered all these shiny
objects, so I'm sure we'll be fine!

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:27.030
Minato!

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:29.400
After all, I'm...

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:34.740
I'm a magic user!

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:49.510
This is me...

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:51.590
I see.

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:54.390
You hadn't realized it, huh?

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:57.890
What do you mean? Since when have I...

00:15:57.890 --> 00:16:00.890
Since the moment we first met.

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:03.730
Then the nurse...

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:06.730
My mom and dad waiting at home...

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:10.280
That girl...

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:14.070
But...

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:17.280
I just need to keep gathering the
shiny objects with you, right?

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:18.540
Then...

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:20.370
It's too late.

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:23.790
The magic I cast on you came undone.

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:27.000
What?

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:30.170
The engine fragment...

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:41.060
If I use that power, I can
even change destiny, right?

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:42.020
Huh?

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:47.690
If there's no potential for me in this world,

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:51.030
then I just need to choose another
potential from the past!

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:55.570
No! The engine is designed to go into the future!

00:16:55.860 --> 00:17:00.160
If you deny your present self,
the magic will become a curse!

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:03.040
What choice do I have but to deny it?

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:06.540
Not a single person cares about me!

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:07.920
Not even that girl...

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:09.590
It was all an illusion!

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:13.670
Everything, even my first hope!

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:18.390
Stop it! Don't curse yourself!

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:21.350
Shut up! You're probably just an illusion, too!

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:30.190
I will change my destiny, no matter what.

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:33.690
I refuse to accept this reality!

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:42.330
<i>I cast aside my only close friend
and pursued the engine fragment.</i>

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:45.290
<i>Even though it seemed within reach,</i>

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:48.000
<i>when I tried to reach out to it,
I found it was far, far away.</i>

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:53.300
<i>My strong emotions cursed me,
and became a dark star.</i>

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:58.550
<i>My consciousness grew hazy, then
cut off, as if swallowed by darkness.</i>

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:03.520
<i>Meanwhile, my other self in the
hospital room fell asleep,</i>

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:06.520
<i>along with several crystallized potentials.</i>

00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:11.570
<i>I don't know how much time passed after that...</i>

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:14.480
<i>But the door opened once again.</i>

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:26.960
<i>The girl who opened the door for me was
the only thing that wasn't an illusion.</i>

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:31.460
<i>Subaru was my one and only hope.</i>

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:35.460
I'm the magic user from back then.

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:39.590
<i>But she doesn't remember
what happened between us.</i>

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:43.390
<i>Even now, I continue to curse myself...</i>

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:47.980
<i>If I disappear, it will all be just an illusion.</i>

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:51.730
<i>The door will never open again.</i>

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:56.490
Soon, the twelfth fragment will come here.

00:18:56.900 --> 00:19:00.490
Once I gather the fragments,
I'll disappear from this world.

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:03.410
No... You can't do that!

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:05.910
Why not? It's not that big a deal, right?

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:09.920
For all of you, it just means losing a hindrance.

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:14.290
Why would you wish yourself to disappear?

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:16.050
It's none of your business.

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:19.510
No, I don't want you to disappear.

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:22.260
Minato!

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:27.020
Minato, you were always helping me...

00:19:27.640 --> 00:19:30.730
You even promised to see the stars with me.

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:34.560
What are you doing?

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:35.770
Look at me.

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:39.690
I'm Subaru.

00:19:40.570 --> 00:19:41.200
Stop it!

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:43.450
How could you undo your
transformation out here?

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:44.570
Do you want to die?

00:19:44.570 --> 00:19:45.950
I remember everything.

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:47.450
I haven't forgotten.

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:49.700
Because I'm a magic user, too!

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:50.460
Stop it!

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:53.080
We traveled into distant space together,

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:57.210
saw a pretty starry sky together,
and talked about lots of things!

00:19:57.500 --> 00:19:58.380
And...

00:19:58.960 --> 00:19:59.800
Stop it!

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:09.770
Minato, let's have strawberry
milk together again...

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:18.190
Subaru,

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:22.700
were you the one who always
continued to open my door?

00:20:23.410 --> 00:20:25.450
You were already so close to me,

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:26.240
but I...

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:27.950
Thank goodness.

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:30.200
You're your usual self.

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:38.340
Minato?

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:42.090
Hope brings me pain...

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:45.010
If I didn't have any hope at all,

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:49.100
I might never have known such agony.

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:50.770
Minato...

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:56.480
You're cursing yourself, too, just like me.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:57.480
Huh?

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:00.030
Somewhere in your heart,

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:05.780
you're actually wishing that collecting the
fragments would never end, aren't you?

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:07.240
That is

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:09.780
your curse upon yourself...

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:17.880
Look at that!

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:22.510
Subarun!

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:25.630
Wonderful! All twelve fragments are there!

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:28.600
Amazing. She really did it all by herself.

00:21:28.600 --> 00:21:29.760
Good job.

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:31.890
Subaru...

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:36.650
Subaru!

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:38.150
Subaru!

00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:40.230
No...

00:21:40.520 --> 00:21:43.900
I haven't been able to change at all.

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:49.910
To Be Continued

00:21:57.080 --> 00:22:01.540
You see, when I looked up

00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:06.930
everyone was smiling at me

00:22:06.930 --> 00:22:16.640
both embarrassed and happy as the starry sky turned sideways

00:22:16.640 --> 00:22:25.610
Ever since then, whenever my daily life seemed hopeless

00:22:20.190 --> 00:22:22.980
...my daily life...

00:22:25.610 --> 00:22:35.370
I'd go into myself just for a little bit and ask

00:22:35.370 --> 00:22:37.250
"Can I fly?"

00:22:37.250 --> 00:22:41.460
"Sky" shall be our meeting point

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:47.090
We can go there whenever we want to

00:22:47.090 --> 00:22:56.770
The wind sows stars in the far distance only light leaps to

00:22:56.770 --> 00:23:01.400
"We have to catch them!"

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:05.900
In the very moment I reached out my hand,

00:23:05.900 --> 00:23:11.240
the scenery around us glittered

00:23:11.490 --> 00:23:15.950
sometime after school

00:23:21.080 --> 00:23:23.880
She always opened my door,

00:23:23.880 --> 00:23:27.210
and at some point, I had accepted that.

00:23:27.210 --> 00:23:27.840
Next episode:

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:30.340
The Final Light
and His Name.

00:23:30.340 --> 00:23:32.970
The dream is at an end now, Subaru.
